1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,606
There are two different connections here.

2
00:00:02,606 --> 00:00:06,712
The K F clamp joins the compression fitting to the welded chamber flange.

3
00:00:06,712 --> 00:00:11,944
The threaded cap at the top has a different job: it compresses an O ring around the gun tube.

4
00:00:11,944 --> 00:00:17,794
I have replaced the single solid placeholder with a separate body, threaded cap, follower and tube seal.

5
00:00:17,794 --> 00:00:23,250
The detailed thread and seal seat are illustrative, pending the actual purchased fitting drawing.

6
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:29,761
First, the fitting body sits on the chamber K F flange, with the face seal between them.

7
00:00:29,761 --> 00:00:33,255
This face seal is separate from the O ring around the tube.

8
00:00:33,255 --> 00:00:37,519
The body is lowered into place, while the compression cap remains loose.

9
00:00:37,519 --> 00:00:41,250
We are showing the mechanical assembly with the chamber vented.

10
00:00:42,550 --> 00:00:45,859
The two clamp jaws close around the mating flange rims.

11
00:00:45,859 --> 00:00:48,447
Tightening the wing nut secures this joint.

12
00:00:48,447 --> 00:00:51,395
From now on, the body stays fixed to the chamber.

13
00:00:51,395 --> 00:00:54,885
You do not loosen this K F clamp to adjust the gun height.

14
00:00:54,885 --> 00:00:58,917
Height adjustment happens at the separate threaded compression cap.

15
00:01:00,217 --> 00:01:05,238
With the upper cap loose, feed the gun service tube upward from inside the chamber.

16
00:01:05,238 --> 00:01:06,812
The gun head stays inside.

17
00:01:06,812 --> 00:01:11,047
The twenty five point four millimetre tube slides through the fitting.

18
00:01:11,047 --> 00:01:16,250
This animation follows the existing gun geometry; the roof and body remain stationary.

19
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:22,536
Now move the complete gun up or down to choose the target to substrate distance.

20
00:01:22,536 --> 00:01:28,331
In our chamber model, the working range is seventy five to one hundred and fifty millimetres.

21
00:01:28,331 --> 00:01:30,201
Here we return to one hundred.

22
00:01:30,201 --> 00:01:32,320
The body and K F clamp stay still.

23
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:34,750
Support the gun while the cap is loose.

24
00:01:36,050 --> 00:01:41,093
Hold the tube at the selected position and turn the cap clockwise, viewed from above.

25
00:01:41,093 --> 00:01:43,348
The cap advances down the body thread.

26
00:01:43,348 --> 00:01:48,450
Its shoulder pushes the follower onto the O ring, squeezing the seal against the tube.

27
00:01:48,450 --> 00:01:50,705
The tube does not rotate with the cap.

28
00:01:50,705 --> 00:01:57,350
The model uses an illustrative two millimetre thread pitch, so two turns produce four millimetres of cap travel.

29
00:01:57,350 --> 00:02:02,333
That is an animation dimension, not a tightening instruction for the purchased part.

30
00:02:03,633 --> 00:02:05,794
The section view shows the load path.

31
00:02:05,794 --> 00:02:10,408
The moving cap shoulder presses the follower, which compresses the tube O ring.

32
00:02:10,408 --> 00:02:13,503
The lower face seal and K F clamp remain undisturbed.

33
00:02:13,503 --> 00:02:19,577
O ring deformation is shown schematically to explain the mechanism; it is not a seal stress calculation.

34
00:02:19,577 --> 00:02:24,833
The actual mating flange and centering ring must also have enough clear bore for the tube.

35
00:02:26,133 --> 00:02:29,866
For a later adjustment, vent the chamber and support the gun.

36
00:02:29,866 --> 00:02:35,435
Loosen only the compression cap, slide the tube to the new position, and retighten the cap.

37
00:02:35,435 --> 00:02:37,270
The K F joint stays assembled.

38
00:02:37,270 --> 00:02:40,575
This is the standalone mechanism animation for review.

39
00:02:40,575 --> 00:02:47,000
The revised CAD includes the separate fitting parts; I have left the previous full walkthrough unchanged.
